A||N||20||fastback87||In need of DRY NOS install instructions||||12||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-21-2001||03:12 PM||||Hey guys I bought a dry nitrous kit (NOS brand) I have a stock 2.8 with original factory injectors and coil.  I am running bosch platinum +4 in all cylinders. :-)  I know how to wire and rewire, It doesn't need to be real basic step by step but I don't know where the vacuum line is supposed to hook up, and why the 50, 75, 90hp jet is in that T fitting instead of at the end of the N20 line.  I also want to know what to do about making sure I don't have a lean cylinder.  I don't have a problem buying new injectors or upgraded injectors, but I don't want to screw my 23mpg when not shooting the juice unless I have to.  <P>Kind of an extra-curricular question.  I would also like to know where the extra fuel comes from in a wet kit and how hard it is to upgrade from dry to wet.||||reg||12
Z||000001||fropuff||11-21-2001||07:11 PM|||| <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS/Page2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/FieroGtNOS/Page2.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sluppy123||11-21-2001||08:58 PM||||The first thing you need to do before you hit the bottle is change out those platinum plugs. N2O and platinum plugs don't play well togeather. <P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost, Eibach Sport springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 17" Mille Miglia's. <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fastback87||11-21-2001||11:49 PM||||so what kind should I use.  I like rapid fire, but they are expensive.  I just freaking bought the +4's and I like AC plugs...are there any other plugs that are better for nitrous?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Shaun41178||11-22-2001||03:33 AM||||hey that is my webpage!!  YEAAA  too bad none of the links on the page work.  I actually had a scanning of the instruction manual on that webpage.  Would have been perfect for you.  <P>You didn't get the instructions from Smoooth?  I mailed them to him.  Ask him as he should have them since he bought the kit from me.<P>The vacuum line for the T fitting gets routed into the vacuum line that goes from the FPr to the Map sensor.<P>The hp jets are not in the T fitting.  They are in a braided steel line that goes from the solenoid to a blue nozzle looking thing.  The line is like 3 feet long and is braided stainless.  The nitrous jet is in that one.  Should be a .036 jet and that is setup for a 70 shot.<P>The stock injectors should be fine.  I never had problems.  If you think you will keep your jets lower then 50 hp or at 50 hp.<P>Wet kit fuel comes from the schrader valves on the fuel rail.  a line is tapped into that and a fuel solenoid is hooked up to it to pump fuel into the intake tract where the nitrous is also shot in.  Its not hard to upgrade at all.  only a solenoid change and a little rerouting of a vacuum line.<P>Email me if you have any quesitons regarding the install of the kit.  I can walk you through it no prob.  <P>Also check out<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Fierogtnos" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/Fierogtnos</A> <P>pics of my nitrous on there somewhere.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||11-22-2001||10:45 AM||||Shaun: I hope you're not angry by me using your page.  I just had it on my bookmarks, so I put it here.  Sorry.  Have a good Thanksgiving!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Smoooooth GT||11-22-2001||12:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B>Hey guys I bought a dry nitrous kit (NOS brand) I have a stock 2.8 with original factory injectors and coil.  I am running bosch platinum +4 in all cylinders. :-)  I know how to wire and rewire, It doesn't need to be real basic step by step but I don't know where the vacuum line is supposed to hook up, and why the 50, 75, 90hp jet is in that T fitting instead of at the end of the N20 line.  I also want to know what to do about making sure I don't have a lean cylinder.  I don't have a problem buying new injectors or upgraded injectors, but I don't want to screw my 23mpg when not shooting the juice unless I have to.  <P>Kind of an extra-curricular question.  I would also like to know where the extra fuel comes from in a wet kit and how hard it is to upgrade from dry to wet.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fastback...    I don't have a clue about the book..  I'll keep looking for it!!! I lost it early on .. That's one reason I never got it completely installed on my car!!!  :sniff,sniff: I never even got to use it...  lol  I'll have another one day.. probablly a wet on though...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
