Z||000013||Shaun41178||11-23-2001||03:50 PM||||No leave the jet in the T fitting htere.  Double check to make sure that it is a .042 jet.  It will have that stamped on the side of the jet.  Again LEAVE THAT JET IN THERE!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It needs to be in there to regulate fuel pressure when the nitrous is activiated.<P>Then I would insert the .032 into the blue spray nozzle that goes into the intake tube.  That is roughly a 50 hp jet.<P>That should be pretty clear.  AGain call me if you need help.||||reg||1
Z||000014||fastback87||11-23-2001||05:36 PM||||Should both jets look excactly the same, minus the size of the hole?  Cause they do.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B>No leave the jet in the T fitting htere.  Double check to make sure that it is a .042 jet.  It will have that stamped on the side of the jet.  Again LEAVE THAT JET IN THERE!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It needs to be in there to regulate fuel pressure when the nitrous is activiated.<P>Then I would insert the .032 into the blue spray nozzle that goes into the intake tube.  That is roughly a 50 hp jet.<P>That should be pretty clear.  AGain call me if you need help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
